<title>FINLAND: FINNISH CENTRE PARTY SAYS NO TO EMU WITHOUT SWEDEN.</title>
<headline>FINNISH CENTRE PARTY SAYS NO TO EMU WITHOUT SWEDEN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's opposition Centre Party said in a report released on Wednesday that Finland should stay out of a narrow monetary union (EMU), but join a broad EMU if it included Britain and Sweden.</p>
<p>Without Sweden it would be cearly better for Finland to stay out of EMU, the report said.</p>
<p>&quot;Under stable economic conditions, the benefits (of EMU membership for Finland) would be bigger than the disadvantages,&quot; said Centre Party MP Mauri Pekkarinen, who chaired the group which compiled the report.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 248</p>
</text>
